      "writtenOn": "2017-09-28T16:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, as far as I can tell, OpenSSH (which can be considered the reference implementation IMHO), is not using it.\nSee user_auth_banner at https://cvsweb.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/auth2.c?rev\u003d1.143\u0026content-type\u003dtext/x-cvsweb-markup for server implementation and input_userauth_banner at https://cvsweb.openbsd.org/cgi-bin/cvsweb/src/usr.bin/ssh/sshconnect2.c?rev\u003d1.266\u0026content-type\u003dtext/x-cvsweb-markup for client.\nAnd I only found two SSH server implementations supporting the language tag for banners: https://github.com/apache/mina-sshd/blob/9dbe5fe084b4e7cbfef62371f881f6c65f26f17b/sshd-core/src/main/java/org/apache/sshd/server/session/ServerUserAuthService.java#L390 and https://github.com/paramiko/paramiko/blob/b27b82c0ba10001d9f67eb7365e1bdc16a19e048/paramiko/auth_handler.py#L239\n\nSo I guess we can drop it.",
      "parentUuid": "241219ae_d1c8c95f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 194,
